{
  "format": 2,
  "cpu": "c14",
  "comment": "SCADA: a level sensor (the knob on I7, 0-10 V) measures a tank. The program turns it into percent (AM1) and fills the tank with the pump on Q1 when the level is 20 % or less, until it is above 80 %. Q2 lights a high-level alarm at 90 %. The screen shows the tank, the level, the pump and the alarm. Turn the knob on the Control Panel to change the level.",
